    {"chapter": "Regulatory Framework", "chapter_num": 10, "question": "Ghana's Anti-Money Laundering Act, 2020 (Act 1044) requires reporting entities to:", "a": "File annual tax returns with the GRA", "b": "Implement CDD/KYC procedures, maintain transaction records, and report suspicious transactions to the FIC", "c": "Maintain a minimum capital requirement", "d": "Publish all client transactions publicly", "answer": "b", "explanation": "Act 1044 mandates AML obligations for reporting entities including customer due diligence, recordkeeping, and STR filing.", "difficulty": "Medium"},
